    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "In the surviving (nu,deg H)=(2,1) stratum, the three tangent multiplicities e_1,e_2,e_3 are pairwise distinct positive integers summing to p and determine all tangent-root ratios by r_i=lambda(e_j-e_k)^(-1). Consequently R(X)=lambda^p(S_e(X/lambda)-S_e(0)) for an explicit S_e in F_p[X] with only critical values 0 and the tangent value. This is a discrete multiplicity normal form plus one scalar conjugacy, not an exclusion, regular-fiber count, or L1 closure.",
